@startuml claim_resolution
title How a chat and a model map to token claims

actor User
participant Token as "oauth_tokens.grants_json"
participant TopicClaim
participant ProviderClaim
participant Topic
participant Chat
participant Provider
participant Model

User -> Token : opaque Bearer
Token -> TopicClaim : topics[]\n{contentClientId, access}
Token -> ProviderClaim : provider?\n{providerClientId, access, contingent}

TopicClaim -> Topic : topic.content_client_id\nin token topic claims
Topic -> Chat : project / topic_projects

ProviderClaim -> Provider : provider.provider_client_id\n== token wallet
Provider -> Model : models.provider_id

note bottom
  Write a node: TopicClaim.access = write for that topic.
  Use a model: ProviderClaim.access in {run, manage}
  and contingent not exhausted.
  Objects (topic, chat, model) stay in the DB.
  Claims name partitions only.
end note

@enduml
